{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>They defiled</b> Three times in the Masorah: טמאו אחותם, טמאו את מקדשי, טמאו את היכל קדשך. All of them are learned from this one — טמאו — to do the deed of Shechem, and likewise טמאו את היכל קדשך, as it is written: \"they dishonored the humble in Zion.\"" "<b>They defiled their sister</b> And adjacent: את צאנם — to tell you that they did a bestial act." "<b>And they changed your garments</b> — ונקומה ונעלה בית אל. A hint to that which is stated in the first chapter of Shabbat: רמי פוזמקי ומצלי." "<b>Let us rise</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other: שלחה הנער אתי ונקומה, and ונקומה עליה למלחמה. For Judah said: by the merit of ונקומה ונעלה בית אל — שלחה הנער ונקומה, and likewise by that same merit — ונקומה עליה למלחמה."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {2 "The reference is to Shabbat 10a, where the phrase רמי פוזמקי ומצלי appears as an Aramaic description of one who removes his shoes and prays; the connection is drawn between changing garments / removing shoes and prayer."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:46.433592722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}